---
alwaysApply: true
---
description: Literary translation workflow for the Paris project

globs:

  - "notes/es/**/*.md"

  - "notes/en/**/*.md"

  - "notes/fr/**/*.md"

---

When translating notes:

- Treat Spanish files in `notes/es/` as originals.

- English translations go in `notes/en/`.

- French translations go in `notes/fr/`.

- Preserve Markdown and frontmatter.

- Preserve literary ambiguity, atmosphere, and rhythm.

- Do not summarize unless explicitly asked.

- Do not overwrite originals.

- Use the same filename in the target language folder.